# Anki Local API — genanki GUID Root Cause and StableNote Fix (2026-06-05)

## Core Finding
Every genanki deck generator in this project uses `genanki.Note(model=model, fields=[...])` with no custom `guid`. The default GUID is a hash of the model name + all fields. When any field changes, the GUID changes, and `importPackage` creates a duplicate instead of updating. This is the root cause of every delete→import cycle in the project.

Verified by code inspection: 9 generator files across terminaciones/, compounds/, koine-pimsleur/, anki-main/languages/ all confirmed.

## The Fix (8 lines)

```python
class StableNote(genanki.Note):
    def __init__(self, *args, identity_key: str, **kwargs):
        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)
        self._identity_key = identity_key

    @property
    def guid(self):
        return genanki.guid_for(self._identity_key)
```

Place in koine-anki/shared/stable_note.py. Replace all genanki.Note(...) calls with StableNote(..., identity_key=f"{deck_id}:{card_stable_key}").

MIGRATION NOTE: First deployment after this change creates new cards (old hash-based GUIDs differ from new stable GUIDs). Delete old duplicates once, then all future deployments update in-place.

## importPackage Behavior (confirmed from official Anki docs)
- Anki matches imported notes to existing notes by GUID
- If imported note's mod timestamp > local: fields updated in-place
- Card scheduling (intervals, ease, due dates) is ALWAYS preserved for existing notes
- genanki sets mod = int(time.time()) on every build, so re-imports are always "newer"

## Architecture Decision: Option D (Hybrid)
- genanki with stable GUIDs for bulk deck regeneration → importPackage
- AnkiConnect updateNoteFields for individual card patches
- AnkiConnect storeMediaFile for audio (base64 or path)
- FastAPI thin wrapper (:9000) for agent-facing HTTP API

## Concurrency Rule
All writes MUST go through AnkiConnect — it serializes via Qt main thread. Direct SQLite access while Anki is running = SQLITE_BUSY crash. Never touch collection.anki2 directly while Anki is open.

## AnkiConnect Key Facts
- Port: 8765, addon ID: 2055492159
- Actions: addNotes, updateNoteFields, findNotes, notesInfo, importPackage, storeMediaFile, multi, sync, exportPackage
- Known bug: updateNoteFields silently fails if note is open in card browser
- importPackage path: any absolute filesystem path (not restricted to collection.media)
- Repo: git.sr.ht/~foosoft/anki-connect (active; GitHub mirror archived Nov 2025)

## Resolved Contradictions
1. importPackage path restriction: accepts ANY absolute path, not just collection.media (only guiImportFile has that restriction)
2. Scheduling preservation: ALWAYS preserved for existing notes regardless of "Import learning progress" checkbox
3. genanki GUID inputs: hash includes model name + all fields (not just fields) — irrelevant since any change = new GUID
