[1mRoot cause confirmed by code inspection (not just research):[22m All 9 generator files across the project use [38;5;10mgenanki.Note(model=model, fields=[front, back])[0m with no custom GUID. The default genanki GUID hashes the model name + all fields, so any content change produces a new GUID → [38;5;10mimportPackage[0m creates a duplicate instead of updating.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe fix is an 8-line class[22m ([38;5;10mStableNote[0m) that overrides the [38;5;10mguid[0m property to hash a stable identity key instead. This eliminates the delete cycle entirely. One-time migration cost: first deploy after the fix will create new cards (old vs new GUID scheme differ), delete the old ones once.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThree contradictions resolved:[22m[0m[0m
1. [38;5;10mimportPackage[0m accepts any absolute path (not restricted to [38;5;10mcollection.media[0m — that's a different action)[0m[0m
2. Scheduling is always preserved for existing notes regardless of the "Import learning progress" checkbox[0m[0m
3. AnkiConnect git.sr.ht repo is active; only the GitHub mirror was archived in Nov 2025[0m[0m
[0m[0m
